      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course! LDL cholesterol is often referred to as 'bad' cholesterol because higher levels can lead to plaque buildup in your arteries, increasing your risk for heart disease. Conversely, HDL cholesterol is called 'good' cholesterol since it helps remove LDL from your arteries, reducing the overall risk for heart issues. Maintaining a healthy balance between the two is important for your heart health.",
